      "content": "Letting the shell go means stopping the performance, which is exhausting because it requires constant energy to maintain a facade that isn't real. You don't have to perform for anyone; the act of pretending is what's draining you, not the world itself. Sometimes, the most honest thing you can do is stop trying to fit into a mold that was never meant for you.",
